1.13.m:
Viṣṇu is the duties, Viṣṇu is the fruits; Viṣṇu is the actions, Viṣṇu is the enjoyer of fruits;
Viṣṇu is the effect, Viṣṇu is the instruments—there is nothing apart from him.

Thus ends the thirteenth chapter, named 'The Discourse on Dharma', in the first quarter of the first part of the glorious Bṛhannāradīya Purāṇa.
